The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (drop)
    iwl_mvm_flush_tx_path(mvm, iwl_mvm_flushable_queues(mvm) & queues, 0);
```
Reason:
The `iwl_mvm_flush_no_vif` function does not hold a mutex when calling `iwl_mvm_flush_tx_path`, which sends a synchronous command to the firmware. This can lead to race conditions and inconsistent states if multiple threads attempt to flush non-STA TX queues simultaneously.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
mutex_lock(&mvm->mutex);
iwl_mvm_flush_tx_path(mvm, iwl_mvm_flushable_queues(mvm) & queues, 0);
mutex_unlock(&mvm->mutex);
```
Reason:
By adding `mutex_lock(&mvm->mutex);` before the call to `iwl_mvm_flush_tx_path` and `mutex_unlock(&mvm->mutex);` after it, the code ensures that the critical section is protected, preventing race conditions and ensuring consistent states when flushing non-STA TX queues.

